{"anchor": {"begin": [127, 0, 464.67], "end": [127, 0, 648.0], "env": "lemma", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 59, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "A.2", "source_sha256": "924155015f3318f4c77548fe50164d381aaa9c11f21acd4655a3f3ff68b5ea50", "statement": "Lemma A.2. Let K = [−1, 1] and suppose a finite family of correction coefficients c ∈ Rm changes the required moments, after taking specified linear combinations of the moments and dividing each resulting component by a specified nonzero factor, by F η (c) = B( η )c + Q η (c, c), η ∈ K. (A.2) Here B and the bilinear map Q are smooth, and B is invertible on K, and the prescribed moment discrepancy is d ∈ C ∞ (K; Rm ). Write β 0 = sup K ∥B −1 ∥, κ 0 = sup K ∥Q∥, and d 0 = ∥d∥ C0(K) . If 8 β 2 0 κ 0 d 0 ≤ 1, there is a unique solution of F η (c) = d( η ) in the ball ∥c∥ C0 ≤ 2 β 0 d 0 . It is smooth in η and is selected by iteration from zero of c ↦→ B( η ) −1 (d( η ) − Q η (c, c)). If Q = 0, there is no smallness requirement. For any preselected finite k, let β k be the operator norm of multiplication by B −1 on C k (K), and let κ k be the corresponding bilinear norm of Q. If also 8 β 2 k κ k ∥d∥ Ck ≤ 1, the same branch satisfies ∥c∥ Ck ≤ 2 β k ∥d∥ Ck . (A.3)", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "high", "coverage": "full", "note": "Under 8β0²κ0d0 ≤ 1 it gives a smooth solution with ‖c‖_{C0} ≤ 2β0d0, uniqueness among continuous solutions in that ball, convergence of the iteration from zero, and ‖c‖_{Ck} ≤ 2βk‖d‖_{Ck} whenever 8βk²κk‖d‖_{Ck} ≤ 1; with Q = 0 the smallness condition holds automatically.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.ClosedIntervalCk.CK": "3919a6e88c89d855fdbd33d7", "NavierStokes.ClosedIntervalCk.I": "bafb926102f6a12646d81cd7", "NavierStokes.ClosedIntervalCk.Jets": "107182ccfa622640b83d395f", "NavierStokes.ClosedIntervalCk.Path":